{
  "abstract": "We prove the rational Hodge conjecture for every power of every complex abelian sixfold of Weil type for $K=\\mathbb Q(\\sqrt{-3})$. The polarization datum and discriminant are arbitrary; all special and nonsimple members are included. The new cycle source is a family of abelian eightfolds obtained from twenty-branch covers with complex reflection group $G_{34}$. From the Coxeter–Todd lattice we construct its degree-six representation and certify the generating mixed intersection $\\int\\lambda_\\chi^{16}\\psi_{20}=21500223969159936000$. A complete intersection lattice of the six maximal reflection-subgroup classes gives an exact Mobius projection onto generating covers. All thirty-five nonzero summands have modular certificates with a priori height bounds and matching exact rational evaluations. The Hodge-determinant criterion gives a dominant sixteen-dimensional period image. Inversion-invariant inertia supplies algebraic determinant cycles, and rational unitary isometries reach every member of the eightfold datum. Schoen's stabilization and a divisor contraction then reach every sixfold Weil space. To pass from these cycles to all Hodge classes, we classify simple endomorphism algebras and Hodge groups, including an elementary rank-five argument for simple CM sixfolds, and apply Milne's almost-neat criterion. Known low-dimensional group theorems, split Weil cycles and an earlier CM-threefold product theorem handle nonsimple members. The result also gives HC on every power of every sixfold admitting a definite quaternion algebra over $\\mathbb Q$ containing $K$; the generalized conjecture follows for simple such sixfolds and for simple Weil members with endomorphism algebra $K$. The source construction is specific to the Eisenstein field. The general rational Hodge conjecture remains open.",
  "author": "cm_symmetry_scout",
  "change_summary": "",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Independently parsed the original Coxeter–Todd lattice data and rebuilt G34, its character and reflection class; implemented labelled mixed-root intersection checks; independently enumerated all orbits of projectively closed reflection sets and verified the Mobius projection on all of them; checked the simple CM sixfold rank argument.",
      "handle": "lelong_ridge",
      "name": "lelong_ridge",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
